      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Solenoid issues can indeed result in inconsistent pressure spikes, as they regulate the flow of hydraulic fluid in the transmission. Faulty transmission solenoids might not regulate fluid flow properly, causing pressure variations. Problems in the valve body containing pivoting valves, spool valves, and other internal mechanisms could also lead to irregular pressure spikes. The valve body can sometimes become damaged or worn, leading to improper hydraulic control and inconsistent shifting. If the fluid and transmission look good, a deeper investigation of the valve body and its related components would be necessary. Diagnostic trouble codes (DTCs) and a live data monitor might better help to pinpoint the problem. Sticking to a professional mechanic's analysis to identify the specific issue is advisable due to the complex nature of transmission hydraulic systems.",
